# Reconnect dropped Modbus clients

Draft · lane full · spec rev 5 · gauntlet green at bbb2222

## Why
A client tab reconnects on its own after the server drops the connection.

## Scenarios
The 1 scenarios of #12: S1 Server restarts during polling

## Stages
- [x] Land spec (aaa1111) <!-- s0 -->
- [ ] Retry with backoff in the client task — in review <!-- s1 blocked-by s0 -->
- [ ] Render reconnecting in the tab — blocked <!-- s2 blocked-by s1 -->
  - beyond unit tests: demo TUI
    - stop the demo server, see "reconnecting", restart it, polling resumes
    - cannot be waived without asking

## Review here
- on the branch: Land spec — inline comments on their files are answered before the next stop
- later stages land after their review and the user's approval

## Requirements
| ID | Issue | Kind | Requirement |
|---|---|---|---|
| MB-R-161 | R1 | new | A TCP client whose connection drops without a user disconnect enters the reconnecting state. |
| MB-R-042 | — | changed · dropped connection no longer ends in disconnected | A TCP client whose connection drops **enters the reconnecting state**. |
| MB-E-031 | E1 | new | A request in flight when the connection drops is lost, not replayed. |
| MB-E-007 | — | dropped | stated "no automatic reconnect"; MB-R-161 replaces it |

### Other spec changes
| File | Section | Change |
|---|---|---|
| modbus/api-contract.md | Client config keys | `reconnect` row, default `true` (MB-R-042) |

## Architecture
1 new, 1 changed components in ferrowl-modbus; `ReconnectPolicy` owned by the client task

| Component | Kind | Crate › module | Change | Role |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ReconnectPolicy` | struct | ferrowl-modbus › client::reconnect | new | backoff 1s to 30s, capped by `max_backoff` |
| `ConnectedCell` | struct | ferrowl-modbus › client | changed | holds a three-state `ConnState` (`Connected`, `Reconnecting`, `Disconnected`) the tab renders |

Public surface:
- `ClientError::Reconnecting`

## Decisions
- reconnecting is its own state (chosen)
- drop it (chosen)
- policy owned by the client task (chosen)
- backoff state lives in the client task (chosen)
- retry forever, no cap (chosen)

Closes #12
exit=0
